From b620af890268450c13a79803abec50dd9500ab43 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John R Reeves III <johnreevesiii@outlook.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 07:00:07 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 2/9] linkbus: multiboard backend seam and opt-in browser
 multiboard

Multiboard now reaches its shared bank, status word, barrier, partner
start and keyboard pipe through linkbus::MultiboardBackend. The native
default is ShmMultiboardBackend in multiboard.cpp: the OS shared memory,
IPC mutex and condition variable, two-phase barrier, os_RunInstance()
partner spawn and keyboard pipe, moved without change of behaviour
(unmasked bank indexing, phase 1 timeout returns early, phase 2 timeout
continues, slave exit throws "Slave exit"). Bank and offset arithmetic
stays in Multiboard.

A host can install a factory (linkbus::setMultiboardFactory); the browser
uses the SAB backend from linkbus_web.cpp. New CMake option
LINKBUS_MULTIBOARD (default OFF) defines NAOMI_MULTIBOARD for Emscripten
builds; the shm backend and the driving simulator spawn stay out of
Emscripten builds. Default builds are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
